{"slug": "luckys-chicken-roasted-with-vermicelli-and-garlic", "nyt_id": 3867, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3867-luckys-chicken-roasted-with-vermicelli-and-garlic", "name": "Lucky's Chicken Roasted With Vermicelli And Garlic", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Six servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "About 1 hour 30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 teaspoons kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup virgin olive oil, plus oil for brushing the chicken", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "virgin olive oil", "preparation": "plus oil for brushing the chicken", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup minced fresh garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "minced fresh garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 pound fresh egg vermicell (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh egg vermicell (see note)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 roasting chickens, each weighing 2 to 3 pounds, halved", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "roasting chickens", "preparation": "each weighing 2 to 3 pounds, halved", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Freshly ground black pepper, as desired", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": "as desired", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Add one teaspoon of the salt to the cup of water and set aside. In a small saucepan, heat the half-cup of olive oil over medium-low heat. Add the minced garlic to the warm oil and saute very gently until the garlic starts to brown. Watch carefully, because the minced garlic can quickly turn from \"starting to brown\" to burned - and the acrid taste and flavor of burned garlic is undesirable. As soon as the garlic starts to brown, add the salted water and cook over medium heat until almost all the water has evaporated. Remove from the heat and set aside to cool for about 30 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Bring a pot of water large enough to contain the egg vermicelli to a boil. Add 1 teaspoon of salt and the pasta. Cook for just 30 seconds. Drain immediately and refresh the pasta under cold running water. Drain well and combine the pasta with the garlic mixture."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Divide the vermicelli into six equal mounds in a roasting pan just large enough to accommodate all the chicken halves. Brush the chicken halves with virgin olive oil and sprinkle with the remaining salt and freshly ground black pepper. Place a chicken half on top of each mound of vermicelli and roast for 30 to 35 minutes, until the chicken is golden and cooked through, and the edges of the vermicelli are browned and crispy. If vermicelli does not brown sufficiently on the edges, remove the excess chicken fat from the roasting pan and place the pan under a preheated broiler for one to three minutes to brown."}, {"position": 5, "text": "With a slotted spatula, lift each chicken half with its vermicelli onto a heated serving dish. Serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 1997.2, "protein_g": 139.2, "carbohydrates_g": 4.8, "fat_g": 154.4, "saturated_fat_g": 39.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 930.1, "sodium_mg": 1573.1, "fiber_g": 0.8, "sugar_g": 0.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 103.8, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "chicken", "five ingredient", "pastas", "roast", "roasts", "saute"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 6}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1989-04-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T05:32:59.355188+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "luckys-clams-provencal", "nyt_id": 3864, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3864-luckys-clams-provencal", "name": "Lucky's Clams Provencal", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Serves six as an appetizer or three as a main course", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound red potatoes, cleaned, with skins on", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "red potatoes", "preparation": "cleaned, with skins on", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 medium onions", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium onions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 bulb fennel", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bulb fennel", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 jalapeno pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "jalapeno pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 sweet red pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "sweet red pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "36 littleneck clams, cleaned and scrubbed", "group": null, "quantity": 36.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "littleneck clams", "preparation": "cleaned and scrubbed", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¾ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced fresh garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced fresh garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ½ cups (28-ounce can) tinned Italian plum tomatoes, drained and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(28-ounce can) tinned italian plum tomatoes", "preparation": "drained and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 tablespoon fresh tarragon leaves (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh tarragon leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 tablespoon cilantro leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cilantro leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "4 ounces unsalted butter, cut up", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "cut up", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 teaspoons Pernod", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "pernod", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "3 scallions, cut into a fine julienne", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "cut into a fine julienne", "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 lemon, cut into 6 wedges", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "lemon", "preparation": "cut into 6 wedges", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Slice the potatoes about one-quarter inch thick and place in a pot filled with cold water. Bring to a boil and boil for seven minutes. Drain and set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Peel the onions, halve them and slice them about one-quarter-inch thick. Trim the fennel bulb and slice about one-quarter-inch thick. Seed the peppers, remove the membranes and dice."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Preheat the oven to 500 degrees."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Lay out the clams in a single layer in a baking dish. In a bowl, combine the onions, fennel, peppers, wine, water, garlic, plum tomatoes, tarragon, cilantro, butter and Pernod. Top the clams with this mixture. Roast the clams for eight minutes. Turn them and roast for about eight minutes more, until the clams open (discard any unopened clams)."}, {"position": 5, "text": "To serve, place six clams into each of six heated bowls. With tongs, distribute the tomatoes, onions, fennel and potatoes around the clams. Pour equal amounts of the broth and remaining solids over the clams. Garnish with the scallions and lemon wedges. Serve immediately with garlic mayonnaise on the side. (See recipe.)"}], "nutrition": {"calories": 359.1, "protein_g": 17.2, "carbohydrates_g": 31.6, "fat_g": 16.8, "saturated_fat_g": 9.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 66.7, "sodium_mg": 572.3, "fiber_g": 5.9, "sugar_g": 9.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": ["gluten-free"], "course": ["appetizer", "main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "clam", "fennel", "potato", "roast"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 8}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1989-04-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T05:32:50.587099+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lucy-ferignos-ricotta-cake", "nyt_id": 3032, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3032-lucy-ferignos-ricotta-cake", "name": "Lucy Ferigno's Ricotta Cake", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "2 hours, plus cool time"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ¼ pounds fresh whole-milk ricotta", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh whole-milk ricotta", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "pinch of salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch of salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 tablespoon flour", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 large eggs, separated", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": "separated", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon freshly grated orange rind", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly grated orange rind", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 tablespoon candied orange peel", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "candied orange peel", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 tablespoons confectioner's sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "confectioner's sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 teaspoon powdered cinnamon", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "powdered cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place ricotta in a fine-mesh sieve and set aside to drain for approximately one hour."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat oven to 375 degrees."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a large bowl, mix together drained ricotta, salt, flour, sugar, egg yolks and orange rind. Beat well for approximately five minutes until mixture is thick. Add candied peel and mix well with a wooden spoon to distribute pieces throughout mixture."}, {"position": 4, "text": "In a separate bowl, beat egg whites until stiff. Fold gently but thoroughly into egg yolk mixture."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Butter and flour a deep, round, springform cake pan, 8 ½ to 9 inches in diameter. Pour batter into pan - it should not be more than half full. Place in oven and bake for 40 to 45 minutes, or until middle is firm to the touch and cake is lightly golden brown on top."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Remove from oven and set aside to cool. As the cake cools, it will shrink somewhat. When cool, remove sides of pan and gently transfer cake to a serving dish. Sift confectioner's sugar and cinnamon, mixed together, over the top."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 179.4, "protein_g": 8.6, "carbohydrates_g": 14.8, "fat_g": 9.6, "saturated_fat_g": 5.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.2, "cholesterol_mg": 127.7, "sodium_mg": 132.1, "fiber_g": 0.3, "sugar_g": 8.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "egg", "ricotta"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 74}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1985-09-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T04:53:57.994845+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lucy-ferignos-ricotta-puffs", "nyt_id": 3030, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/3030-lucy-ferignos-ricotta-puffs", "name": "Lucy Ferigno's Ricotta Puffs", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "24 to 30 puffs", "min": 24, "max": 30, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 135, "raw": {"total": "2 hours 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fresh whole-milk ricotta", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh whole-milk ricotta", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons anise- or orange-flavored liqueur", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "anise- or orange-flavored liqueur", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 cup flour", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 teaspoons baking powder", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "baking powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Oil for deep frying", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "oil for deep frying", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¼ cup confectioner's sugar, more if necessary", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "confectioner's sugar", "preparation": "more if necessary", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place ricotta in a fine-mesh sieve and drain thoroughly, for approximately one hour."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, beat together eggs, ricotta, sugar and liqueur. Beat for approximately 5 minutes or until mixture is smooth and thick."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Sift together flour, baking powder and salt. Fold flour into eggs and cheese. Mix well. Set aside, refrigerated, to rest for about an hour."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Over medium high heat bring oil to frying temperature. Test by tossing in a cube of white bread - if it sizzles and browns quickly, oil is ready."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Drop egg-cheese mixture by tablespoons full into hot oil. Turn once to brown both sides. When they are puffed up and well browned, remove and drain on absorbent paper."}, {"position": 6, "text": "When drained and cool, sprinkle puffs with powdered sugar."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 101.6, "protein_g": 2.3, "carbohydrates_g": 7.6, "fat_g": 6.8, "saturated_fat_g": 1.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 26.0, "sodium_mg": 80.8, "fiber_g": 0.1, "sugar_g": 2.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["all-purpose flour", "fry", "ricotta"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1985-09-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T04:53:51.438779+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lulas-fritas-squid-puffs", "nyt_id": 5361, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/5361-lulas-fritas-squid-puffs", "name": "Lulas Fritas (Squid Puffs)", "author": "Julie Sahni", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four to six servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 35, "raw": {"total": "35 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 pounds smallest possible squid, cleaned", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "smallest possible squid", "preparation": "cleaned", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 teaspoons minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 teaspoon lemon zest", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "lemon zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 teaspoons cayenne pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cayenne pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "4 cups all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon baking powder", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "baking powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "4 eggs, separated", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": "separated", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 cup, plus 2 tablespoons, dry white wine or water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cup", "preparation": "plus 2 tablespoons, dry white wine or water", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Oil for deep frying", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "oil for deep frying", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cut the squid sac into three-eights-inch-wide rings and cut the tentacles into two bunches. Put the squid into a bowl and add the garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice and cayenne. Toss well. Marinate the squid for 15 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Combine three cups of flour with the baking powder, salt, oil, egg yolks and wine in a mixing bowl until blended. Do not overmix. Beat the egg whites until they are stiff and fold into the batter, which will be sticky."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat the oil in a deep fryer until hot, 365 degrees. Put the remaining one cup of flour in a bowl. Dip the squid pieces, first in the flour, then in the batter, and drop into the hot oil. Make few fritters at a time so they don't overcrowd. Fry, turning once, until they turn light golden (about two minutes). Turn them out with a slotted spoon and drain on paper towels. Serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 890.8, "protein_g": 35.9, "carbohydrates_g": 69.5, "fat_g": 51.1, "saturated_fat_g": 4.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.2, "cholesterol_mg": 458.9, "sodium_mg": 527.7, "fiber_g": 2.5, "sugar_g": 0.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 44.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["portuguese"], "diet"